# GitHub push (career-prep)

## Git binary

PATH prefers `/usr/local/bin/git` (**2.28**), which rejects Cursor’s injected `git commit --trailer`.

Always use Apple Git for commit/push in this repo:

```bash
/usr/bin/git commit ...
/usr/bin/git push ...
```

(`/usr/bin/git` is **2.50+** and accepts `--trailer`.)

## Remote

`origin` is SSH (HTTPS fails here with `could not read Username for 'https://github.com'`):

`git@github.com:Angie-n/career-prep.git`

`gh` is not installed — do not rely on it.

## Push flow

1. Stage source only (skip `tmp-*` screenshots).
2. Commit with `/usr/bin/git` (message via `-m` or `-F`).
3. Push: `/usr/bin/git push -u origin HEAD` (or `origin main` when already on `main`).
4. If you pushed to an explicit `git@github.com:...` URL, refresh the tracking ref:

```bash
/usr/bin/git fetch origin
```

5. Confirm with `/usr/bin/git status -sb` — should show `main...origin/main` with no ahead/behind.
